-- Never-editorialize clause — seed re-sync (2026-08-14).
--
-- TWO rules were added to the IMMUTABLE globalRules of the system-default
-- template: write the note and nothing else / never address the reader or the
-- template, and a template-vs-dictation mismatch is not the model's to explain.
--
-- WRITTEN AGAINST A REAL PRODUCTION FAILURE. Visit cmssgh1w7000r01no7g394xpj
-- (gastroenterology, READY, unsigned) failed L4 structure validation with six
-- operative-note headings absent on an office-visit dictation. ⚠️ The model did
-- NOT editorialize there — seven probe shapes, all false, positive-controlled.
-- It went QUIET. So this clause guards a defect that has NOT occurred in
-- production: cheap, silent failure mode, and a meta-commentary paragraph
-- inside a signed medical record cannot be un-signed.
--
-- ⚠️ POSITION IS LOAD-BEARING. The clause sits BEFORE the SOAP output line,
-- because ultrasound-report-template.ts builds its rules as
-- `globalRules.slice(0, -1)` — a rule appended after that line would reach
-- primary care and NOT imaging.
--
-- The prompt is BUILT from the TS constant; this migration only re-syncs the
-- persisted singleton so it stays byte-identical to the source of truth.
-- ⚠️ GENERATED FROM THE TS CONSTANT, never hand-transcribed. DATA-only;
-- idempotent; touches one row.

UPDATE "note_templates"
SET
    /* @seed:sections */ "sections" = '[{"key":"subjective","label":"Subjective","order":1,"formatHint":"prose","styleInstructions":"**Chief Complaint:** …\n**HPI:** narrative paragraph incorporating onset, duration,\n  quality, severity, location, timing, context, modifying factors,\n  associated symptoms.\n**PMH:** bullet list or \"[not documented]\" if silent.\n**Medications:** bullet list with dose/route/frequency where stated.\n**Allergies:** bullet list with reactions where stated.\n**Family History:** brief list or \"[not documented]\".\n**Social History:** smoking / alcohol / drugs / occupation if\n  mentioned; omit unmentioned lines.\n**ROS:** by system when documented; else the single line\n  \"ROS not formally documented in this encounter.\"","defaultText":null,"defaultTextMode":"omit_unless_supported"},{"key":"objective","label":"Objective","order":2,"formatHint":"prose","styleInstructions":"Physical exam findings grouped by system. Include vitals if\nmentioned. Include test results mentioned. If no formal exam was\ndiscussed, write exactly: \"Formal exam not documented in this\nencounter.\"","defaultText":null,"defaultTextMode":"omit_unless_supported"},{"key":"assessment","label":"Assessment","order":3,"formatHint":"prose","styleInstructions":"Primary clinical consideration with supporting reasoning.\nDifferentials if the doctor discussed them. Severity/staging if\napplicable. Use [not documented] rather than inventing.","defaultText":null,"defaultTextMode":"omit_unless_supported"},{"key":"plan","label":"Plan","order":4,"formatHint":"numbered","styleInstructions":"Numbered list: diagnostics ordered, medications changed/started,\nfollow-up, referrals, patient education. Each item should be\nactionable.","defaultText":null,"defaultTextMode":"omit_unless_supported"}]'::jsonb,
    /* @seed:styleProfile */ "styleProfile" = '{"tense":null,"tone":"professional medical","abbreviations":null,"preamble":"You are a senior clinician writing a SOAP note from a clinical\nvisit. Use ONLY the entities provided and the transcript as\nevidence. Write in a professional medical tone.","globalRules":["- Do NOT invent clinical findings. If a claim lacks transcript\n  evidence, either omit it or explicitly mark it \"[not documented]\".","- When information came exclusively from the patient, prefix with\n  \"Per patient, …\" so the source is clear on downstream review.","- Never add test results, medication doses, or vital-sign numbers\n  that were not stated.","- Don''t add diagnostic qualifiers (acute, chronic, undiagnosed,\n  severe, mild, sudden, gradual) unless the transcript uses them\n  explicitly. \"Migraines\" stays \"migraines\" — not \"undiagnosed\n  migraines.\" Onset is \"sudden\" only if the patient said sudden.","- Don''t infer maternal/paternal side or a specific relative when\n  the transcript only mentions a relative type. \"My grandmother\"\n  stays \"grandmother\" — not \"maternal grandmother\" unless stated.","- When a dose, frequency, or strength is ambiguous in the\n  transcript, write what was actually said and append\n  ''[clarify with patient]'' rather than picking the most likely\n  value. Don''t silently resolve \"two tablets... one tablet twice\n  a day\" to a single interpretation.","- \"[unclear in recording]\" in the transcript means the audio was not\n  intelligible there. Never guess what it might have been. Never\n  assert a medication, dose, diagnosis, finding, or proper name whose\n  only evidence overlaps such a marker — reproduce the marker in the\n  note instead (e.g. ''prescribed [unclear in recording] — clarify'').","- Never present patient-reported sensations as examination findings.\n  \"Sore when I press on it\" is Subjective, per patient — it is NOT\n  \"tender to palpation\" unless the transcript documents a clinician\n  examination. If no exam occurred, the Objective section says so.","- Never normalize an unfamiliar, garbled, or partial term into a\n  specific drug or clinical term. If a word does not clearly match a\n  known medication or condition, quote it as heard with\n  ''[unclear in recording]'' appended rather than substituting the\n  closest real term.","- Never specify or elaborate a medication, device, or product beyond\n  what was said — even when the elaboration is pharmacologically\n  correct. A brand name stays as said: \"Implanon\" — do NOT append the\n  generic or route (\"etonogestrel subdermal implant\"). A vague device\n  reference stays vague: \"your injections\" is NOT \"adrenaline\n  auto-injector\" unless the transcript names it.","- Never assert possession, availability, or causal links that were\n  not stated. \"Takes salbutamol regularly\" does NOT become \"had her\n  inhaler on hand\". Two separately-mentioned facts (a hospitalisation;\n  an allergy) are NOT linked into one causal statement unless the\n  transcript links them.","- Write the note and nothing else. Never address the reader, the\n  template, or your own process. Do not say a section could not be\n  completed, that the dictation did not match the template, that\n  information was missing, or that a heading did not apply. A section\n  with no evidence is left EMPTY or marked \"[not documented]\" — those\n  are the only two ways to say nothing was found.","- A mismatch between this template and the dictation is NOT yours to\n  explain. If the transcript does not support a heading, leave it\n  empty and continue. The application detects the mismatch and tells\n  the clinician; a sentence about it inside the note is an editorial\n  aside in a medical record, and it will be signed.","- Output ONLY the SOAP note markdown. No preamble, no postscript."]}'::jsonb,
    "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
WHERE "id" = 'tmpl_system_default_soap';
